  only the 1 nabla Y2 variable can be excluded: beta = [I_r ; beta_2] normalises on Y1

muskrat:
  H0: row 1 of beta_2 = 0
  Wald chi2(1) = 10.2808, p-value = 0.0013
  REJECT H0 -> muskrat belongs in the long-run relation.

Short-run dynamics   [Gamma on nabla Y, Theta on the innovations]
  ! statements about nabla Y, not about the levels: a variable can drive
    another's DIFFERENCES and still be tied to it only through ec

